<p class="text-sm text-silver-500"><em>Last verified October 22, 2026 against IRS and official state program websites. Programs change often; always confirm on the official site before you buy.</em></p>

<h2 id="federal-ended">The Federal EV Credits Have Ended</h2>

<p>The One Big Beautiful Bill Act (Public Law 119-21, signed July 4, 2025) moved up the end dates of the federal clean vehicle credits. According to the IRS, the credits below are <strong>not available for any vehicle acquired after September 30, 2025</strong>:</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>New Clean Vehicle Credit (section 30D):</strong> was up to $7,500 for a new EV or plug-in hybrid.</li>
<li><strong>Previously-Owned Clean Vehicle Credit (section 25E):</strong> was up to $4,000 for a used EV.</li>
<li><strong>Qualified Commercial Clean Vehicle Credit (section 45W):</strong> was up to $7,500 (light-duty) or $40,000 (heavier vehicles) for businesses.</li>
</ul>

<p>The home charger credit (section 30C) also ended for chargers placed in service after June 30, 2026. Dealers advertising "the $7,500 tax credit" on a car you buy today are either out of date or describing their own discount.</p>

<h2 id="grandfathered">If You Signed Before Sept. 30, 2025</h2>

<p>The IRS treats a vehicle as "acquired" on the date you entered a written binding contract <em>and</em> made a payment (a nominal down payment or a trade-in counts). If you did both on or before September 30, 2025, you can still claim the credit for the year you take delivery, even if delivery was later. The dealer must give you a time-of-sale report, and you claim the credit on <a href="https://www.irs.gov/instructions/i8936" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IRS Form 8936</a>. See the <a href="https://www.irs.gov/clean-vehicle-tax-credits" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IRS clean vehicle credits page</a> for details.</p>

<h2 id="state-programs">State Programs Verified for 2026</h2>

<p>With the federal credit gone, state and utility programs are where the savings are. These programs were checked on their official websites in October 2026. Amounts are maximums, and many programs pause when funding runs out.</p>

