<p>For every other state, and for city, county and utility programs, search the U.S. Department of Energy's <a href="https://afdc.energy.gov/laws/state" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Alternative Fuels Data Center</a>. Our <a href="/states/">state pages</a> also cover registration fees, insurance minimums and EV rules where you live.</p>

<h2 id="other-savings">Other Ways to Save on an EV in 2026</h2>

<ul>
<li><strong>Utility rebates and EV rates:</strong> Many electric utilities pay toward a Level 2 home charger and offer off-peak rates that make overnight charging much cheaper. Check your utility's website.</li>
<li><strong>Automaker and dealer incentives:</strong> With the federal credit gone, many brands offer their own cash-back or low-APR financing. Compare these with the price before you negotiate.</li>
<li><strong>Leasing:</strong> Lease deals sometimes include manufacturer support. Read the money factor and residual, not just the monthly payment.</li>
<li><strong>Used EVs:</strong> Used EV prices have fallen. Decode the VIN with our <a href="/">free VIN checker</a> to confirm the exact trim and battery, check for open recalls, and get a vehicle history report before you buy.</li>
<li><strong>Insurance:</strong> EV insurance can cost more than for comparable gas cars, so compare quotes before you buy.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="how-to-claim">How to Claim State Rebates</h2>

<ol>
<li><strong>Check the program is open</strong> and has funding on the official website.</li>
<li><strong>Confirm the vehicle qualifies:</strong> MSRP caps, range minimums and new-versus-used rules vary.</li>
<li><strong>Get pre-approval if required.</strong> Income-qualified programs such as Clean Cars 4 All and Charge Up+ often require you to apply before you buy.</li>
<li><strong>Buy from a participating dealer</strong> when the rebate is applied at the point of sale (New York, New Jersey, Connecticut, Massachusetts).</li>
<li><strong>Apply on time</strong> for post-purchase rebates (for example, Illinois requires applications within 180 days).</li>
<li><strong>Keep your documents:</strong> purchase or lease contract, registration and proof of residency.</li>
</ol>

